Q: How to write a UTF-8 file with Java? A: <h2>tl;dr</h2>
<p>In Java 8+, <code>Files.write</code> defaults to <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UTF-8" rel="nofollow noreferrer">UTF-8</a>.</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>Files.write(
    Paths.get(&quot;/path/to/foo.txt&quot;), 
    List.of(&quot;These&quot;, &quot;are&quot;, &quot;lines&quot;)
)
</code></pre>
<h2>Java NIO</h2>
<p>As part of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-blocking_I/O_(Java)" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Java NIO</a>, the Java 7 <a href="http://docs.oracle.com/javase/7/docs/api/java/nio/file/Files.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>Files</code></a> utility type is useful for working with files:</p>
<pre><code>import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.nio.file.Files;
import java.nio.file.Path;
import java.nio.file.Paths;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.util.*;

public class WriteReadUtf8 {
  public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
    // Inputs.
    List&lt;String&gt; lines = Arrays.asList(&quot;These&quot;, &quot;are&quot;, &quot;lines&quot;);

    // Write file.
    Path textFile = Paths.get(&quot;foo.txt&quot;);
    Files.write(textFile, lines, StandardCharsets.UTF_8);

    // Read file.
    List&lt;String&gt; read = Files.readAllLines(textFile, StandardCharsets.UTF_8);

    // Dump to console.
    System.out.println(lines.equals(read));
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>The <a href="http://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/java/nio/file/Files.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Java 8 version</a> allows you to omit the <code>Charset</code> argument - the methods default to UTF-8.</p>
<pre><code>Files.write(textFile, lines);  // Defaults to UTF-8.
</code></pre>
<p>By the way, most features in <a href="https://openjdk.org/jeps/400" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Java 18+ default to UTF-8</a>.</p>
<h2>Modern Java</h2>
<p>In recent versions of Java, that entire <code>WriteReadUtf8.java</code> file can be reduced to:</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>void main() throws IOException {
    // Inputs.
    List&lt;String&gt; lines = List.of(&quot;These&quot;, &quot;are&quot;, &quot;lines&quot;);

    // Write file.
    Path textFile = Paths.get(&quot;foo.txt&quot;);
    Files.write(textFile, lines);

    // Read file.
    List&lt;String&gt; read = Files.readAllLines(textFile);

    // Dump to console.
    lines.forEach(IO::println);
}
</code></pre>
